@startuml
title Digital Credential Issuance (SD-JWT VC, HSM-backed Issuer, On-Device Credential Model)

participant User
participant "Mobile App / Wallet" as App #lightblue
participant "DW Core" as DW #lightcyan
participant "Government API Source of Truth" as Agency #lightgray
participant "VCVP Adapter" as Adapter #palegreen
participant "VCVP Core" as Core #lightgreen
participant "one-core (Credential Engine)" as Engine #orange
participant "HSM" as HSM #yellow
participant "Trust Registry ETDA" as Trust #violet

note over Adapter,Trust #wheat:[SPEC] endpoint NN = endpoint number in index.html (index-1.html uses its own numbers)\nDW endpoint NN = endpoint number in index-dw.html (DW Core API)

note over Engine,HSM #wheat:[SPEC] Issuer signing keys are HSM-backed\nPrivate key is generated inside HSM\nPrivate key never leaves HSM\nEngine stores key metadata and HSM reference\nVCVP Core receives ISSUER_KEY_ID and publicKey only\n[IN DEVELOPMENT] engine v1.86.1 key storage supports only INTERNAL , AZURE_VAULT , SIGN8\nSECURE_ELEMENT , REMOTE_SECURE_ELEMENT , no HSM , PKCS11 removed since v1.78.2

note over User,App #lightblue: 1.1 User Login
User->App: Login (PIN / biometric to unlock wallet)
App->App: [PENDING] Login with government digital ID (Tang Rat / ThaID)\nobtain IdP ID token (pid , ial , auth_time , amr if provided)

note right of App #wheat:[PENDING] For team discussion : the wallet does not send identity assurance to DW today\nHow the wallet logs in and obtains the IdP ID token is part of the wallet, the wallet\nteam must decide where the code is exchanged

note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Wallet Activation runs at first login on this device (separate sequence)\nregisters holder key in DW (POST /dw/v1/holder-keys/challenge (DW endpoint 01) , POST /dw/v1/holder-keys/register (DW endpoint 02))\n→ device status = HOLDER_BOUND

note over App,DW #lightblue: 1.2 Request VC Issuance
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] A card/document is added to the wallet only when both conditions hold\n1. applicant data is linked from the government source of truth (section 2)\n2. the VC is issued and verified by the wallet (sections 8 , 9)\nAny problem in VC issuance returns an error to the wallet , the wallet stops\nNo card/document is added without a VC
App->App: Check holder key exists on this device\n(key alias in Android Keystore / Secure Enclave)
alt Holder key not found on device
    App->App: Run Wallet Activation section 2 (see Wallet Activation flow)\ncreate holder key and register it in DW\n(POST /dw/v1/holder-keys/challenge (DW endpoint 01) , POST /dw/v1/holder-keys/register (DW endpoint 02)) , then continue
else Holder key found
    App->App: Continue
end
note right of App #wheat:[SPEC] Key found on the device does not confirm it is registered in DW\nDW checks registration by deviceId below
App->DW:Request to add card / document + Token | POST /v1/virtualcards/sync_queue_list (DW endpoint 03)\n(deviceId)\n[PENDING] + IdP ID token
App-->User: Show processing (wait for response of 1.2)
DW->DW: Validate Token → CitizenId
DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store issuance request in DW database
note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW database (issuance request)\nissuanceSessionId (created by DW)\nCitizenId (from Token)\ndeviceId\nrequested card / document\nstatus\nrequestedAt
DW->DW: Look up holder key of this device in DW database\n(deviceId → device status = HOLDER_BOUND)

alt Holder key of this device not registered
    DW->DW: Mark VC not possible (reason = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED)\nno response yet , the error is returned in section 2.1
    note right of DW #wheat:Response of 1.2 tells the app to register the holder key again (Wallet Activation section 2)\nso the next request can receive the card/document with a VC
else Holder key registered
    DW->DW: Continue to 1.3
end

note over DW #lightblue: 1.3 Validate Existing Identity Assurance

alt IdP ID token provided (PENDING)
    DW->DW: [PENDING] Load IdP signing keys (IdP jwks_uri , cached)
    DW->DW: Verify ID token\nsignature (IdP JWKS , ES256) , iss = IdP , aud = client_id registered with the IdP , exp , nonce
    DW->DW: Check pid in ID token = CitizenId from Token

    alt ID token invalid / pid mismatch
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = IDENTITY_ASSURANCE_INVALID
        DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (reason = IDENTITY_ASSURANCE_INVALID)
        App<--DW: Reject issuance request\nreason = IDENTITY_ASSURANCE_INVALID
        App-->User: Cannot proceed , please log in again
    else ID token valid
        DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store identity assurance profile in DW database
        note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW database (identity assurance profile)\nial → IAL level\niss → KYC source\nauth_time → last authentication timestamp\namr → last authentication method (if provided)\npid → citizenId\nissued ID token reference (jti) → audit
    end
else No IdP ID token (existing session)
    DW->DW: Use identity assurance profile stored at last login
end

DW->DW: Load existing identity assurance profile

note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Identity assurance profile in DW database\nidentityAssuranceId\ncitizenId\nIAL level\nAAL level\nKYC source\nKYC timestamp\nassurance expiry\nlast authentication method\nlast authentication timestamp

DW->DW: Check VC possible for this request (mark set in 1.2)
alt VC already marked not possible in 1.2 (WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED)
    DW->DW: Skip RequiredLoA check and step-up\n(the request already failed in 1.2 , it ends with an error in section 2.1)
else VC still possible
    DW->DW: [PENDING] Get RequiredLoA of the requested document from DW catalog\n(DocumentSchemas.RequiredLoA via document-schemas/list)
    note right of DW #wheat:[PENDING] RequiredLoA is set by the issuing agency on the schema\nNot taken from the Trust Registry , its LoA support is not known yet
    DW->DW: Validate assurance\nstill valid (assurance expiry) , meets required freshness ,\nIAL level ≥ RequiredLoA

    alt Assurance invalid / expired / not fresh / IAL below RequiredLoA
        App<--DW: Request step-up verification or re-KYC\nreason , RequiredLoA
        App-->User: Complete additional verification (e.g. ThaID)
        App->DW: [NEW] Submit verification result (new IdP ID token) | POST /dw/v1/identity-assurance/step-up (DW endpoint 04)
        DW->DW: Verify new ID token (same checks as above)
        DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store updated identity assurance profile in DW database
        DW->DW: Validate assurance again

        alt Still not sufficient
            DW->DW: Mark VC not possible (reason = LOA_INSUFFICIENT)\nthe error is returned in section 2.1
        else Assurance sufficient
            DW->DW: Continue to Read Data
        end

    else Assurance valid
        DW->DW: Continue to Read Data
    end
end

note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Use user session\nuserId\ncitizenId\naccess token

note over DW,Agency #lightgray: 2. Read Official card / document
DW->DW: Look up applicant data in DW database

alt No data in DW database
    DW->Agency:Fetch applicant data from agency

    note right of Agency #wheat:[SPEC] Retrieve official card/document data\nfrom government source of truth

    alt Data not found / not authorized
        DW<--Agency: Not found | Not authorized
        DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (reason = AGENCY_DATA_NOT_FOUND / AGENCY_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
        App<--DW: Return reason (Not found 404 | Not authorized 403)
        App-->User: Show reason (Not found 404 | Not authorized 403)
    else Agency data available
        DW<--Agency: Applicant data + SyncDate
        DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store applicant data + SyncDate in DW database
        note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW database\nsourceFetchedAt = SyncDate\nsourceLastUpdatedAt = from agency if available\nsourceSystem = Government API Source of Truth\ncachePolicy = reuse data in DW database if it already exists\ncacheKey = citizenId + documentType\ncacheInvalidation = on revoke / suspend / expire
    end

else Data already exists
    DW->DW: Use applicant data from DW database
end

DW->DW: Validate official data & Check status active & Check not suspended &\nCheck not revoked etc.

alt Official card/document invalid
    DW->DW: Update status SOURCE_DATA_INVALID
    DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (reason = SOURCE_DATA_INVALID)
    App<--DW: Reject issuance request
    App-->User: card/document not eligible
else Official card/document valid
    DW->DW: Prepare verified claims
end

note over App,DW #lightgray: 2.1 Check VC is possible before issuing
DW->DW: Check VC possible for this request (mark set in 1.2 / 1.3)
alt VC not possible (WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED from 1.2 / LOA_INSUFFICIENT from 1.3)
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED / LOA_INSUFFICIENT\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (reason = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED / LOA_INSUFFICIENT)
    App<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED / LOA_INSUFFICIENT\nnextAction = REGISTER_HOLDER_KEY (only when reason = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED)
    App-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
    App->App: If reason = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED : run Wallet Activation section 2\n(POST /dw/v1/holder-keys/challenge (DW endpoint 01) , POST /dw/v1/holder-keys/register (DW endpoint 02))\nso the user can request the card/document again
    note over User,App #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 3 to 11 do not apply
else VC possible
    DW->DW: Continue to Trust Framework Validation
end

note over DW,Trust #violet: 3. Trust Framework Validation
note right of Adapter #wheat:[SPEC] Endpoints 06 , 10 , 11 , 14 are shared with agency systems that call the VCVP Adapter directly\n(system to system , separate sequence) , not only with DW Core\nSteps marked "caller channel = WALLET" run only for requests from DW Core\nDW Core returns the error to the app , VCVP Core only returns the reason
DW->Adapter: [NEW] Get schema details | POST /vcvp-adapter/v1/document-schemas/get
Adapter->Core: Get schema details | POST /vcvp/v1/document-schemas/get (endpoint 06)
Core->Core: Validate caller authorization
note right of Adapter #wheat:[SPEC] VCVP Adapter writes its own access log (gateway level) for every request\nincluding requests it rejects itself (e.g. invalid Consumer-Key) , these never reach VCVP Core\nVCVPAuditLog holds only requests that reach VCVP Core
alt Caller not authorized
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of endpoint 06 (reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
    Adapter<--Core: 403 | reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    DW<--Adapter: 403 | reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    App<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    App-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
    note over User,App #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 3 to 11 do not apply
else Caller authorized
    Core->Core: Continue to trust validation
end
Core->Trust: [NEW] Validate issuer eligibility and schema policy | GET {trust registry URL}
Trust-->Core: Trust status policy LoA requirement

Core->Core: Keep trust validation result (→ audit record of endpoint 06)
note right of Core #wheat:[AUDIT LOG] VCVPAuditLog (TrustCheck)\ntrust validation result → TrustCheck.Result\npolicy version → TrustCheck.PolicyVersion\ntimestamp → TrustCheck.CheckedAt\ntrust registry reference → TrustCheck.RegistryReference\nLoA requirement → TrustCheck.LoARequirement\nWritten once with the audit record of endpoint 06 , never updated

Core->Core: Validate issuer allowed & schema approved

alt Trust validation failed
    Core->Core: Update status TRUST_FAILED
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of endpoint 06 (reason = TRUST_FAILED , TrustCheck , EngineCalls)
    Adapter<--Core: Reject issuance request\nreason = TRUST_FAILED
    DW<--Adapter: Reject issuance request\nreason = TRUST_FAILED
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = TRUST_FAILED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    App<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = TRUST_FAILED
    App-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
    note over User,App #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 3.1 to 11 do not apply
else Trust validation passed
    Core->Core: Continue to Read Schema
end

note over DW,Engine #orange: 3.1 Read Schema
Core->Core: Look up card/document schema in DocumentSchemas table
alt Schema not found
    Core->Core: Update status SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of endpoint 06 (reason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND , TrustCheck , EngineCalls)
    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] The credential schema must be created by the issuing agency (endpoint 05)\nVCVP does not create a schema during issuance
    Adapter<--Core: 404 | reason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND
    DW<--Adapter: 404 | reason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    App<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND
    App-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
    note over User,App #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 4 to 11 do not apply
else Schema found
    Core->Core: Map DocumentSchemaId → engine CREDENTIAL_SCHEMA_ID\n(DocumentSchemas.EngineRefs[].RefDocumentSchemaId)
    Core->Core: Check the agency allows requests from the wallet on this schema\n(DocumentSchemas.AllowWalletRequest)\nonly when caller channel = WALLET (DW central Consumer-Key)

    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core requests system to system with one central Consumer-Key for all agencies\nThe agency opts in per schema when creating it (endpoint 05)\nChecked again in endpoint 10

    alt Wallet request not allowed by the agency
        Core->Core: Update status WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of endpoint 06 (reason = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED , TrustCheck , EngineCalls)
        Adapter<--Core: 403 | reason = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED
        DW<--Adapter: 403 | reason = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
        App<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED
        App-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
        note over User,App #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 4 to 11 do not apply
    else Wallet request allowed
        Core->Core: Continue to read schema details
    end
end
Core->Engine: Get schema details | GET /api/credential-schema/v2/{id} (endpoint 06)
Core<--Engine: 200 | schema details + Claims[] (ClaimId | Path | Name | Type | Required)
Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of endpoint 06 (TrustCheck , EngineCalls)
Adapter<--Core: 200 | schema details + Claims[] (ClaimId | Path | Name | Type | Required)\n+ IssuerTrust (Result , CheckedAt , RegistryReference) from TrustCheck
DW<--Adapter: 200 | schema details + Claims[] + IssuerTrust
DW->DW: Keep IssuerTrust (→ response of 1.2 , preview in section 7.2)

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Defined on the schema , not on the issuance request (engine name → DocumentSchemas field)\nformats[] sets the format to SD_JWT_VC (→ Formats[].Format)\nallowSuspension must be set to true explicitly , otherwise the credential cannot be suspended (→ Suspendable)\nRevocation method is not stored in the schema , it comes from config that binds SD_JWT_VC to TOKENSTATUSLIST (→ Formats[].RevocationMethod)\nEach claim has a technicalKey separate from key , e.g. LicenseNumber -> license_number (→ Claims[].Path , Claims[].Mappings[].TechnicalKey)\nThe name that appears in the credential is the technicalKey

note over DW #lightgreen: 4. Prepare Data
DW->DW: Map data to Claims[] based on schema details from endpoint 06\nSet OrgCode of the issuing agency\n(IssuerIdentityId and IssuerKey are not sent , VCVP Core selects them in section 5.1)

note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Map fields to claim IDs

DW->DW: Create tamper-proof audit record

note right of DW #wheat:[AUDIT LOG] auditHash = hash(canonical audit payload)\nauditSignature = sign(auditHash)\npreviousAuditHash = link to previous log\nretentionPolicy = e.g. 10 years or regulatory requirement\nretentionUntil = issuedAt + retention period\nimmutableStorage = WORM / append-only log

DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store mapped claims + audit log in DW database (issuance request)
note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW database\nissuance request\nmapped claims\naudit log\nidentity assurance reference

note over DW,Core #lightgreen: 5. Request Issuance and Validate Request
DW->Adapter: [NEW] Request credential issuance (VC) | POST /vcvp-adapter/v1/documents
Adapter->Core: Request credential issuance | POST /vcvp/v1/documents (endpoint 10)
Core->Core: Validate caller authorization\nallowed to issue this VC type on behalf of this organisation\n(caller channel WALLET : DocumentSchemas.AllowWalletRequest = true)
Core->Core: Validate tenant scope\nreferenced data belongs to the caller's organisation
Core->Core: Validate claims against schema | Validate key matches identity (if sent)\nCitizenId → CitizenHashId

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Claim name restrictions are enforced at schema creation , not at issuance\nName must not be "0" | must not contain / because it separates nested claim levels\nTotal key length must not exceed 255 characters

note right of Core #wheat:[PENDING] Issuer key lifecycle is not decided yet\nEngine key has no status or expiresAt (only id , createdDate , lastModified , organisationId\nname , publicKey , keyType , storageType , isRemote , autogenerated)\nACTIVE / DEPRECATED status must be stored in the VCVP Keys table\nKeep old key available for verifying previously issued credentials\nOld key status = DEPRECATED, not revoked\nUse new key for new credential issuance only\nRevoke old key only if compromised

alt Request invalid / unauthorized
    Core->Core: Update status = REQUEST_REJECTED
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of endpoint 10 (reason = REQUEST_REJECTED)

    note right of Core #wheat:[ERROR AUDIT] failureStep = VALIDATE_REQUEST\nerrorCode\nerrorMessage\nretryable = true/false\nfailedAt\nissuanceSessionId\nuserId

    Adapter<--Core: Reject issuance request
    DW<--Adapter: Reject issuance request
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = REQUEST_REJECTED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    App<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = REQUEST_REJECTED
    App-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
else Request valid
    Core->Core: Continue issuance
end

note over Core,HSM #orange: 5.1 Check Issuer Setup

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Organisation , issuer key and DID must be prepared by the issuing agency in the setup phase (endpoint 01 , 02 , 03)\nVCVP does not create them during issuance\nIf any of them is missing , VC is not issued and the card/document is not added

Core->Core: Look up agency organisation in Organizations table (OrgCode)
Core->Core: Select issuer DID from the schema\n(DocumentSchemas.IssuerIdentityId)\nuse IssuerIdentityId instead if the caller sent it
Core->Core: Select issuer key = the ACTIVE key of that DID\n(Keys.Status = ACTIVE , Keys.IdentityId)\nuse IssuerKey instead if the caller sent it

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Issuer key status : RESERVED / ACTIVE / DEPRECATED / REVOKED\nRESERVED = key placed in the DID at creation , not used for signing yet\nOnly one ACTIVE key per identity (unique index on IdentityId + Status = ACTIVE)\nNo ACTIVE key → handled in section 5.2 (switch to the next RESERVED key)\nMore than one ACTIVE key → configuration error , do not guess\nVCVP Core always sends issuer and issuerKey to the engine , never relies on the engine default (first key in the DID)

alt Organisation / issuer DID not found , or more than one ACTIVE key
    Core->Core: Update status = ISSUER_SETUP_NOT_FOUND
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of endpoint 10\n(reason = ORGANISATION_NOT_FOUND / ISSUER_DID_NOT_FOUND / ISSUER_KEY_AMBIGUOUS)
    Adapter<--Core: Reject issuance request\nreason = ISSUER_SETUP_NOT_FOUND
    DW<--Adapter: Reject issuance request\nreason = ISSUER_SETUP_NOT_FOUND
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUER_SETUP_NOT_FOUND\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    App<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = ISSUER_SETUP_NOT_FOUND
    App-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
    note over User,App #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 5.2 to 11 do not apply
else Organisation and issuer DID found , at most one ACTIVE key
    Core->Core: Use ORG_ID , ISSUER_IDENTIFIER_ID , ISSUER_KEY_ID (ACTIVE key , if any)
end

Core->Core: Update issuance status = READY_FOR_ISSUANCE

note over Core,HSM #orange: 5.2 Credential Lifecycle Policy and Issuer Key Check

Core->Core: Read credential metadata & validFrom & validUntil &\nrevocation status method & credential lifecycle policy from schema / config\nand record in Documents table

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Validity is defined on the schema (expiration) , not per credential\nRevocation method comes from config bound to the format (SD_JWT_VC → TOKENSTATUSLIST)

Core->Core: Get issuer key metadata from VCVP Keys table\nkey status , createdAt , expiresAt

note right of Engine #wheat:[SPEC] DID can have multiple keys (verification methods)\nAll keys must be included when the DID is created (up to 5)\nEngine has no identifier update API (only POST , GET , DELETE , list , /remote)\nKeys cannot be added to an existing DID\nKeys can be rotated without changing DID by switching issuerKey to a key already in the DID

alt No ACTIVE key / key expired / near expiry / inactive

    alt Next key reserved in the issuer DID is available
        Core->Core: Switch issuerKey to the next reserved key in the DID\n(Keys.Status RESERVED → ACTIVE)
    else No reserved key left in the DID
        Core->Core: Update status = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of endpoint 10 (reason = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED)

        note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] VCVP does not create a new key or DID during issuance\nThe existing DID cannot be updated , so new keys need a new DID\nThe issuing agency creates the new key and DID in the setup phase (endpoint 02 , 03)\nand registers the new DID in the Trust Registry before use

        Adapter<--Core: Reject issuance request\nreason = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED
        DW<--Adapter: Reject issuance request\nreason = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
        App<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED
        App-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
        note over User,App #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 6 to 11 do not apply
    end

    Core->Core: Mark old ISSUER_KEY_ID as DEPRECATED

    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Keep old ISSUER_KEY_ID available for verifying previously issued credentials\nOld key status = DEPRECATED, not revoked\nUse new ISSUER_KEY_ID for new credential issuance only\nRevoke old key only if compromised

else Key active
    Core->Core: Continue issuance
end

note over Core,Engine #orange: 6. Create Digital Credential and Offer
Core->Core: Map VCVP ClaimId to engine claim id
Core->Engine: Create credential | POST /api/credential/v1 (endpoint 10)\ncredentialSchemaId , issuer = agency IdentifierId (did:web) , issuerKey\nprotocol = OPENID4VCI_FINAL1\nclaimValues [ claimId , path , value ]
Engine-->Core: { id } = CREDENTIAL_ID

note right of Engine #wheat:[IMPORTANT] Nothing is signed at this step , no status list index is reserved and no token exists yet\nState is CREATED and the credential field is empty\nThis request has no format , proofType , cnf or revocation method parameter\nformat and revocation method come from schema and config | cnf comes from the wallet proof at credential request\nissuer takes the engine IdentifierId , not the did:web value\nCredential expiry cannot be set per credential

Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store document in Documents table
note right of Core #wheat:[DATA STORE] Documents table\nCREDENTIAL_ID → EngineRefs[].RefDocumentId (+ EngineRefs[].EngineName)\nDocumentSchemaId , IssuerOrganizationId , IssuerIdentityId , CitizenHashId , SyncDate
Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of endpoint 10 (EngineCalls)
Adapter<--Core: 200 | DocumentId

Adapter->Core: Request offer link | POST /vcvp/v1/documents/offer (endpoint 11)
Core->Core: Validate caller authorization
alt Caller not authorized
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of endpoint 11 (reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
    Adapter<--Core: 403 | reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    DW<--Adapter: 403 | reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    App<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    App-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
    note over User,App #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , sections 7 to 11 do not apply
else Caller authorized
    Core->Core: Continue to create offer link
end
Core->Engine: Create offer link | POST /api/credential/v1/{CREDENTIAL_ID}/share (endpoint 11)
Engine-->Core: url = openid-credential-offer://?credential_offer_uri=...\nexpiresAt

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] credential_offer_uri points to\n/ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/offer/{credentialId}\nThe offer contains credential_issuer , credential_configuration_ids (the vct URL)\nand grants.pre-authorized_code\ntransaction_code is not used , so the offer has no such field\nEngine state changes from CREATED to PENDING after this call

Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store offer in Documents table
note right of Core #wheat:[DATA STORE] Documents table\nCREDENTIAL_ID → EngineRefs[].RefDocumentId\nurl → OfferUrl (temporary)\nexpiresAt → OfferExpiresAt\nStatus = PENDING\nissuance status = pending / claimed / expired / cancelled\nScheduled background job updates expired offers

Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of endpoint 11 (EngineCalls)
Adapter<--Core: 200 | OfferUrl + ExpiresAt
DW<--Adapter: 200 | DocumentId + OfferUrl + ExpiresAt
DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store DocumentId + OfferUrl + ExpiresAt in DW database (issuance request)
App<--DW: 200 (response of 1.2) | issuanceSessionId , OfferUrl , ExpiresAt\nissuerTrust (Result , CheckedAt , RegistryReference)

note over App,Engine #orange: 7. Wallet Resolves Credential Offer

note right of App #wheat:[SPEC] OpenID4VCI 1.0 section 13.4 Split-Architecture Wallets\nThe app resolves the offer itself , DW Core only passes the OfferUrl and never holds the pre-authorized_code\n(13.4 : a server component with access to pre-authorized codes MAY be able to impersonate the application)\nIssuer trust check is done on the app (design choice , 13.5 requires the Wallet to validate the Credential Issuer)

App->App: Parse OfferUrl → credential_offer_uri

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Protocol endpoints (/ssi , /.well-known) carry no Consumer-Key\noffer , token , credential , notification write VCVPAuditLog (Actor Channel = WALLET , no caller OrgCode)\nissuer metadata , authorization server metadata , nonce , DID document , vct type metadata are public reads\nrecorded only in the access log , not in VCVPAuditLog


App->Adapter: [NEW] Read offer from credential_offer_uri | GET /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/offer/{credentialId}
