        note over Engine,HSM #f4cccc: 8.3 Issuer Signs the Credential (signing point 2)

        Engine->Engine: Reserve an index in the Token Status List\nget { uri , idx } and embed it as status in the token
        Engine->Engine: Embed holder public key from the proof as cnf
        Engine->Engine: Build SD_JWT_VC and compute _sd digests of selectively disclosable claims

        Engine->HSM: Sign SD-JWT (JWS) with issuer signing key (ECDSA / ES256)
        HSM-->Engine: Issuer signature (private key never leaves HSM)

        note right of Engine #wheat:[SIGNING POINT 2] Signed token structure\nheader : typ = dc+sd-jwt , alg = ES256\nkid = verificationMethod id of the issuer did:web , format did:web:...#key-{keyId}\npayload : vct , vct#integrity , iss = issuer did:web\niat , nbf , status.status_list = { uri , idx } (Token Status List)\ncnf.jwk = holder public key , raw EC P-256\n_sd = digests , _sd_alg = sha-256\nDisclosures appended with ~ , each is [ salt , technicalKey , value ]\n\nsub is present only when the holder uses a DID identifier\nWith a KEY identifier , as chosen , there is no sub and no holder DID anywhere in the credential\nexp is present only when credential validity is configured , otherwise only iat and nbf

        note right of Engine #wheat:[SIGNING POINT 2] Required setup , otherwise signing fails\n1. The issuing key must be declared in the DID Document under assertionMethod\nthe engine looks up kid in this relationship , signing fails if not found\n2. The vct URL must be resolvable , by default the engine hosts it at /ssi/vct/v2/{orgId}/{schemaId}/SD_JWT_VC\nif moved to our domain it must still resolve\n3. The Token Status List must be published and resolvable at /ssi/revocation/v1/list/{id}\nthe list is a JWT signed with the same issuer key

        Engine->Engine: State OFFERED → ACCEPTED
        Engine-->Core: SD_JWT_VC (signed) + all disclosures + notification_id
        Core->Core: Documents = ACTIVE

        note over Core #lightgreen: 8.4 Issuance Audit Log
        Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of /ssi credential (eventType = CREDENTIAL_ISSUED , EngineCalls)

        note right of Core #wheat:[AUDIT LOG] eventType = CREDENTIAL_ISSUED\ncredentialId\nvct\nissuedAt\nissuer identifier (did:web) + signing kid\nholder key reference + cnf thumbprint (not a DID)\ncredential status reference = uri + idx\nnumber of proofs received in the request (batch)\nauditHash , auditSignature , previousAuditHash , retentionUntil\nno personal data claims in the audit trail

