        App<--Adapter: Credential (SD_JWT_VC + all disclosures) + notification_id
        App->App: Keep notification_id (→ notification in section 9)\nRead iss and kid from the credential (→ issuer DID document)\nRead vct from the credential (→ vct type metadata)

        note over App #lightblue: 9. Wallet Verifies Before Storing
        note right of App #wheat:[SPEC] Goal : the app checks the credential is genuine and usable before saving it\nCheck 1 : the issuer really signed it and nothing was changed (see the note under Verify issuer signature)\nCheck 2 : the issuer is trusted (issuer DID (iss) is listed in the Trust Registry and its accreditation has not expired)\nCheck 3 : the credential is bound to this phone (holder key in the credential (cnf.jwk) = the key on this device)\nCheck 4 : the credential type is the one offered and its description was not changed (vct , vct#integrity)\nAny check fails : tell the engine (credential_failure) and DW (issuance_result FAILED) , the card/document is not added\nAll checks pass : save the credential (9.1 , 9.2) , tell the engine (credential_accepted) and DW (issuance_result ACCEPTED) (9.3)
        App->Adapter: [NEW] Get issuer DID document from iss (did:web) | GET /ssi/did-web/v1/{id}/did.json
        Adapter->Core: Get issuer DID document | GET /ssi/did-web/v1/{id}/did.json
        Core->Engine: Get issuer DID document | GET /ssi/did-web/v1/{id}/did.json (endpoint 49)
        Engine-->Core: DID document
        Adapter<--Core: DID document
        App<--Adapter: DID document
        App->App: Verify issuer signature (Check 1)\nusing the public key of the verificationMethod matching kid
        note right of App #wheat:[SPEC] Goal : prove the credential was signed by the issuer and was not changed\nRequired by RFC 9901 (SD-JWT) section 7.2 , done on the app because only the app receives the full credential\nStep 1 : read from the credential the signing key id (kid) and the issuer (iss)\nStep 2 : check the key belongs to the issuer (the DID before # in kid = iss)\nStep 3 : in the issuer DID document (request above) , find the public key whose id = kid\nStep 4 : check that key is allowed to sign credentials (kid is listed in assertionMethod)\nStep 5 : give the credential and that public key to an SD-JWT library , it checks the signature and every disclosure\nLibrary : eudi-lib-jvm-sdjwt-kt (Android) , eudi-lib-sdjwt-swift (iOS) , sd-jwt-js (JS)\nWith the Procivis wallet SDK , steps 1 to 5 run inside issuance-accept\nAny step fails → Verification failed branch below
        App->Trust: [NEW] Check issuer DID (iss) is listed and accreditation not expired (Check 2) | GET {trust registry URL}
        Trust-->App: Accreditation status
        App->App: Check cnf.jwk matches the public key of the key on this device (Check 3)
        note right of App #wheat:[SPEC] Why the holder key is checked now (Check 3)\nThe credential works only with the key whose public key is in cnf.jwk\nIf that is not the key on this device , the user can never present this credential to a verifier\n(the app cannot create the key binding proof (Key Binding JWT) that the verifier requires)\nCheck it here before saving , not later when the user presents the credential
        App->Adapter: [NEW] Get credential type description from the vct URL in the credential (vct type metadata) | GET /ssi/vct/v2/{orgId}/{credentialSchemaId}/SD_JWT_VC
        Adapter->Core: Get credential type description (vct type metadata) | GET /ssi/vct/v2/{orgId}/{credentialSchemaId}/SD_JWT_VC
        Core->Engine: Get credential type description (vct type metadata) | GET /ssi/vct/v2/{orgId}/{credentialSchemaId}/SD_JWT_VC (endpoint 50)
        Engine-->Core: credential type description (vct type metadata)
        Adapter<--Core: credential type description (vct type metadata)
        App<--Adapter: credential type description (vct type metadata)
        App->App: Check the credential type (Check 4)\nvct in the credential = the credential type that was offered (credential_configuration_id)\nhash of the credential type description just downloaded = vct#integrity in the credential

        alt Verification failed / issuer DID not trusted
            App->DW: [NEW] Report issuance result + Token | POST /v1/virtualcards/issuance_result (DW endpoint 06)\n(issuanceSessionId , result = FAILED , reason = VERIFICATION_FAILED / ISSUER_NOT_TRUSTED ,\nnotification_id , access token , notification_endpoint)
            DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
            DW->Adapter: [NEW] Notify credential_failure with notification_id + access token | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification (notification_endpoint)
            Adapter->Core: Notify credential_failure with notification_id + access token | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification
            Core->Engine: Notify credential_failure with notification_id + access token | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification (endpoint 48)\nevent = credential_failure
            note right of Engine #wheat:[SPEC] OpenID4VCI 1.0 notification : credential_failure is used for unsuccessful cases not caused by a user action\ncredential_deleted is used only when the user caused it
            Engine->Engine: State ACCEPTED → ERROR
            Engine-->Core: 204
            Core->Core: Update status = ISSUANCE_FAILED
            Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of /ssi notification (reason = VERIFICATION_FAILED / ISSUER_NOT_TRUSTED , event = credential_failure)
