        else Verification passed

            note over App #lightblue: 9.1 Credential Storage Model (on device or cloud)
            note right of App #wheat:[PENDING] Two storage modes are kept in the design , one will be removed later\nIn both modes the holder private key stays on the device
            alt Storage mode = ON_DEVICE
                App->App: [DATA STORE] Store the full token (SD_JWT_VC + disclosures) in the on-device database
                App->App: [DATA STORE] Store credential metadata in on-device database
                note right of App #wheat:[DATA STORE] on-device database\ncredentialId , credentialType , vct\nissuer DID / issuer display name\nschemaId\nvalidFrom / validUntil\nstatus reference ( uri + idx )\ndisplay metadata
                App->App: Bind credentialId to holder key reference\nBind credentialId to deviceId
                App->App: Mark credential as available for presentation

                note right of App #wheat:[SPEC] On-device credential model\nThe wallet owns the full token , so it can present offline\nand does not disclose data to backend systems when presenting a VP\nHolder private key remains on device\nBackend does not keep the full VC , only references
            else Storage mode = CLOUD (encrypted on the device before upload)
                App->App: Encrypt the full token (SD_JWT_VC + disclosures) on the device\nwith a data key protected by secure hardware (Secure Enclave / Android Keystore)
                App->DW: [NEW] Store encrypted credential + Token | POST /dw/v1/credentials (DW endpoint 08)\n(credentialId , encrypted token , credential metadata)
                DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store encrypted credential in DW cloud storage
                note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW cloud storage\nCitizenId , deviceId , credentialId\nencrypted token (DW cannot decrypt it)\ncredential metadata : credentialType , vct , issuer DID , validFrom / validUntil , status reference ( uri + idx )
                App<--DW: 201 | cloud reference
                App->App: [DATA STORE] Store credential metadata + cloud reference in on-device database
                App->App: Bind credentialId to holder key reference\nBind credentialId to deviceId
                App->App: Mark credential as available for presentation

                note right of App #wheat:[SPEC] Cloud credential model\nThe token is encrypted on the device , DW stores only ciphertext and metadata\nTo present a VP the app downloads the ciphertext , decrypts it on the device and signs with the on-device key\nPresenting needs a network connection\nHolder private key remains on device
                note right of App #wheat:[PENDING] Recovery of the data key when the device is lost or replaced\nWhether credential metadata on DW may be stored in clear\nEndpoint name POST /dw/v1/credentials (DW endpoint 08) is a placeholder
            end

            note over App #lightblue: 9.2 Secure Local Storage and Access Policy
            note right of App #wheat:[SPEC] Applies to the on-device database in both modes\nIn CLOUD mode it holds credential metadata and the cloud reference , not the full token
            App->App: Use secure local storage for the on-device database (from 9.1)
            note right of App #wheat:[SPEC] Secure local storage\nAndroid : EncryptedSharedPreferences / Room encrypted DB\niOS : Keychain
            App->App: Encrypt the database with envelope encryption\nKEK in secure hardware protects DEK on disk , DEK encrypts the data files
            App->App: Set file protection so data is unreadable while the screen is locked\nnot only until first unlock after boot
            App->App: Protect credential access with device security\nbiometric / PIN / device unlock
            App->App: Store only the personal data that is necessary\ndo not keep readable claim copies without justification
            App->App: Prevent export of holder private key\nSecure Enclave / Android Keystore / StrongBox
            App->App: Configure usage policy\nrequire holder confirmation before presentation\nrequire holder signing before VP submission

            note right of App #wheat:[SPEC] Target is OWASP MASVS-STORAGE level L2\nThe library provides only L1 , the gap must be implemented

            note over App,Engine #lightblue: 9.3 Wallet confirms receipt
            App->DW: [NEW] Report issuance result + Token | POST /v1/virtualcards/issuance_result (DW endpoint 06)\n(issuanceSessionId , result = ACCEPTED , notification_id , access token , notification_endpoint)
            DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ACCEPTED
            DW->Adapter: [NEW] Notify credential_accepted with notification_id + access token | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification (notification_endpoint)
            Adapter->Core: Notify credential_accepted with notification_id + access token | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification
            Core->Engine: Notify credential_accepted with notification_id + access token | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification (endpoint 48)\nevent = credential_accepted
            Engine-->Core: 204 (state stays ACCEPTED)
            Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store wallet receipt confirmation in Documents table
            Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of /ssi notification (event = credential_accepted)
            Adapter<--Core: 204
            DW<--Adapter: 204
            DW->DW: Prepare card/document data from applicant data (section 2)
            App<--DW: 200 (response of issuance_result) | digital card/document data
            App->App: [DATA STORE] Store card/document data in on-device database\nlinked to the stored credentialId
            note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Two ways are supported to send credential_accepted\n1. The app calls the notification endpoint directly (App → Adapter , same path)\n2. The app reports to DW and DW sends the notification (used in this flow)\nWay 2 : the app passes notification_id , access token and notification_endpoint to DW\n(OpenID4VCI 1.0 section 11 : the Wallet MUST present a valid access token to the Notification Endpoint)\nDW acts as the server-side component of the Wallet (section 13.4)

            note right of Engine #wheat:[SPEC] The engine sets ACCEPTED when the credential is issued , not on notification\ncredential_accepted does not change state\ncredential_failure → ERROR | credential_deleted → REJECTED

            App-->User: Show digital card/document with a VC badge\n(card/document data from DW , linked to the stored verifiable credential)
        end

    end

else Holder rejects credential
    User->App: Reject
    App->DW: [NEW] Reject offer + Token | POST /v1/virtualcards/offer_reject (DW endpoint 07)\n(issuanceSessionId , reason = HOLDER_REJECTED)
    DW->Adapter: [NEW] Reject credential | POST /vcvp-adapter/v1/wallet/offers/reject
    Adapter->Core: Reject credential | POST /vcvp/v1/wallet/offers/reject (endpoint 14)
    Core->Core: Validate caller authorization
    alt Caller not authorized
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of endpoint 14 (reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
        Adapter<--Core: 403 | reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
        DW<--Adapter: 403 | reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
        note over DW,Core #wheat: Reject not recorded in VCVP , the offer still expires by itself
    else Caller authorized

        note over Core #pink: 11. Handle Holder Reject
        Core->Core: Update status HOLDER_REJECTED\ndo not call engine , let the offer expire
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of endpoint 14 (reason = HOLDER_REJECTED)

        note right of Core #wheat:[ERROR AUDIT] eventType = CREDENTIAL_REJECTED\ncredentialId\nuserId\nholder key reference\nissuer identifier\nrejectionReason\nrejectedAt\nauditHash\nauditSignature\npreviousAuditHash\nretentionUntil\nimmutableStorage = WORM / append-only

        Adapter<--Core: 200
        DW<--Adapter: 200
    end
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = HOLDER_REJECTED
    App<--DW: Cancel issuance
    App-->User: Credential not issued , card/document not added
end


@enduml
